WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.718
"This is NeuPL, or Neural Population Learning,

00:00:04.798 --> 00:00:09.516
published at ICLR 2022 by researchers at University
College London and DeepMind.

00:00:09.596 --> 00:00:14.313
Learning to play strategy games like StarCraft or
poker requires discovering a whole population of diverse policies,

00:00:14.393 --> 00:00:19.111
not just one.

00:00:19.191 --> 00:00:23.909
The usual recipe grows this population by
iteratively training a fresh policy to beat the previous ones,

00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:28.707
but in real games that approach wastes compute
relearning basic skills at every step and

00:00:28.787 --> 00:00:33.504
produces under-trained policies when budgets run out.

00:00:33.584 --> 00:00:38.302
NeuPL solves both problems by representing the
entire population inside a single conditional neural network,

00:00:38.382 --> 00:00:43.100
so skills transfer freely across policies while
still enjoying convergence guarantees."
